Joseph N. Hall wrote:

> Hi. I'm wondering, what relatively simple evolutionary tweaks and
> features would you like to see added to NetHack?
> 
> I feel like adding a few things without making any major gameplay
> changes. Currently, a new set of objects

FWIW, I would consider new objects and YANIs relating to upgrading "useless"
objects to be major changes. Useless objects serve an important purpose in
NetHack: they make it harder to find good objects. They are the noise from
which the player must glean the signal.

New objects have the opposite effect: they reduce the frequency of existing
objects, unless you increase the total number of objects generated. That
might actually be a good thing, considering that half the fun of NetHack is
the identifying and sorting phase, but it needs careful balancing.

